The form sections live in the right column of a two-column grid; the page scrolls (body scroll). Sections are tall. IntersectionObserver-based scrollspy tracks heading visibility — works for body scroll. Manual fallback: on window scroll, compute active section by rect.top. Both are ~15 lines. To keep tests simple (FormNav is stubbed in panel tests anyway), I'll do:

