where fallbackScrollspy is a local composable returning activeHeadings ref + updateHeadings no-op. FormNav uses activeHeadings to highlight. I'll also expose `updateHeadings` — FormNav needs a ref to the headings elements to pass. With useScrollspy, you must call `updateHeadings(elements)` after mount and whenever sections change. Since our sections are static, one call on mounted. Fallback scroll spy: listen to scroll → compute.

