content.thinking:
Now I see it!

```js
const rootProps = useForwardProps(reactivePick(props, "as", "unmountOnHide"), emits);
```

`useForwardProps` with `useEmitAsProps(emits)` — this converts the EMITS into props, i.e., creates `{ onUpdate:modelValue: ... }`? Let me check `useEmitAsProps`:

```js
export function useEmitAsProps(emits) {
  const result = {};
  for (const key in emits) {
    result[`on${capitalize(key)}`] = emits[key];
  }
  return result;
}
```

Hmm — `emits` is the Vue emit function (from setup). `for (const key in emits)` — iterating over a function's enumerable keys — typically none! So emitAsProps = {} → rootProps = { as, unmountOnHide } only.

Then TabsRoot receives:
- `v-bind="rootProps"` → { as, unmountOnHide }
- `:model-value="props.modelValue"`
- `:default-value="props.defaultValue"`

TabsRoot emits `update:modelValue` — but NO ONE listens to it in the nuxt/ui Tabs wrapper!! There's no `@update:model-value` handler! So when reka's TabsRoot emits update:modelValue, the nuxt/ui Tabs component does NOT re-emit it upward!

Wait — but then how does the REAL app's v-model work with UTabs?? Let me look at the full Tabs.vue template again:

```vue
<TabsRoot
  v-bind="rootProps"
  :model-value="props.modelValue"
  :default-value="props.defaultValue"
  :orientation="props.orientation"
  :activation-mode="props.activationMode"
  ...
```

Hmm — if reka TabsRoot's `changeModelValue` sets `modelValue.value` via useVModel → which EMITS update:modelValue — and nobody listens... the value never propagates. That would mean nuxt/ui v4 Tabs v-model is broken?! Unlikely — more likely `useEmitAsProps(emits)` DOES produce the listener. Let me check useEmitAsProps in reka-ui:

Actually, reka-ui's useEmitAsProps:

```js
export function useEmitAsProps(emits) {
  const result = {};
  for (const key in emits) {
    result[`on${capitalize(key)}`] = emits[key];
  }
  return result;
}
```

Hmm — `for (const key in emits)` — emits is a function; functions have no enumerable own properties... UNLESS Vue attaches the emit function with properties. In Vue 3.6 (rc), the `emits` function from setup context — hmm. Actually wait — in the nuxt/ui Tabs source, `emits` comes from `defineEmits(["update:modelValue"])` — the emit function. `for (const key in emits)` iterates enumerable properties — a plain function has none (no enumerable props). So emitAsProps = {}.

Hmm, then how does nuxt/ui Tabs v-model work at all?! Let me look at reka-ui's useEmitAsProps source to be sure.

